course: dictionary
lesson: 1979
title: Calm words: composedly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Composedly is an adverb, a word that tells you how something is done. It means in a calm, steady way, with your feelings under control. You can answer composedly, wait composedly, or walk composedly.
explain: Look at the clues around it. In Alice, the strange creatures could frighten anyone. «Alice answers the strange creatures composedly» tells us she does not panic. Her steady answers show she is in control of her feelings.
explain: Two related words help too: composed means calm, and composure means calmness. If you know that calm is the idea, you can work out composedly. Then swap in your meaning, "calmly", and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Composedly means calmly, in a steady way with your feelings under control.
fact: Composed means calm, and composure means calmness.
fact: Adverbs like composedly often end in -ly and tell you how something is done.
fact: «Alice answers the strange creatures composedly» shows that Alice is not afraid.
fact: Calmly is a close synonym. Nervously is the opposite, because it means worried and unsteady.
exercise: Alice answers the strange creatures «composedly». What does composedly mean? | Nervously, shaking with fear | Loudly, shouting over them all | *Calmly, with her feelings under control | Sleepily, with her eyes closed
exercise: Composure is a word about calm. What does composure mean? | Anger that boils over | *Calmness, with feelings under control | Deep sleep | Great speed
exercise: The old man stayed composed when the storm hit. Which word is closest in meaning to composed? | Hungry | *Calm | Noisy | Sunny
test: A girl hears a strange noise in the dark and waits composedly for the lights to come on. How does she wait? | *Calmly, with her feelings under control | Crossly, stamping her feet | Sadly, with her head down | Loudly, calling for help
test: Which sentence uses composedly correctly? | The baby cried composedly all night. | *The coach stood composedly at the side of the pitch, though the match was in chaos. | She tripped composedly over the step and fell. | The boy shouted composedly at the dog.
exam: Which word means the opposite of composedly? | *Nervously | Calmly | Steadily | Patiently
